Open Falsification License v1.0
==============================

Copyright (c) 2026 Advanced Propulsion Physics Laboratory

Preamble
--------

This license is designed for scientific software and frameworks that make
extraordinary claims. It extends the freedoms of open-source licensing with a
reciprocal obligation: if you use this work, you must preserve its capacity to
be falsified. The right to prove something wrong is as sacred as the right to
prove it right.

The Open Falsification License (OFL) guarantees that no derivative work, patent,
or commercial arrangement may suppress, obscure, or circumvent the falsification
mechanisms embedded in this software. It ensures that negative results, null
findings, and refutations carry the same legal standing and distribution rights
as positive confirmations.


Section 1 — Definitions

  "Work" refers to the software, documentation, data, equations, diagrams, and
  all other materials covered by this license.

  "Falsification Mechanism" means any module, test, assertion, logging facility,
  or documented protocol whose purpose is to detect, measure, or report when the
  Work's claims fail — including but not limited to: null-hypothesis checks,
  ablation studies, boundary-condition validators, statistical significance
  tests, noise-floor measurements, and reproducibility checklists.

  "Covered Claim" means any empirical prediction, numerical threshold, or
  physical assertion made by or on behalf of the Work, whether in source code,
  documentation, or accompanying publications.

  "Derivative Work" has the meaning given in applicable copyright law, and
  includes any modification, extension, or adaptation of the Work.

  "You" means any person or entity exercising permissions granted by this
  license.


Section 2 — Granted Permissions

  Subject to the conditions in Sections 3–6, You are hereby granted a
  worldwide, royalty-free, non-exclusive right to:

  a) Reproduce the Work in any medium or format.

  b) Modify the Work, create Derivative Works, and distribute them under the
     terms of this license.

  c) Use the Work for any purpose, including commercial applications, provided
     that the conditions of Sections 3–6 are met.

  d) Publish results — whether positive, negative, or inconclusive — obtained
     through the use of the Work, without fear of legal retaliation.

  e) Develop and distribute competing or alternative models that reference the
     Work, provided attribution is given as specified in Section 4.


Section 3 — Falsification Preservation Condition

  This is the core condition of the OFL. Any Derivative Work that You
  distribute must:

  a) Retain all Falsification Mechanisms present in the original Work, or
     provide functionally equivalent replacements that test the same Covered
     Claims with equal or greater statistical power.

  b) Not disable, bypass, obscure, or weaken any Falsification Mechanism by
     default. Falsification Mechanisms may only be deactivated through an
     explicit, documented, and user-visible configuration option that clearly
     states the scientific implications of deactivation.

  c) Include a "FALSIFICATION.md" file (or equivalent) that:
     i.   Lists all Covered Claims testable by the software.
     ii.  Describes how to run each Falsification Mechanism.
     iii. States the criteria under which each Covered Claim is considered
          falsified.
     iv.  Provides a template for reporting null or negative results.

  d) If You add new Covered Claims to the Derivative Work, You must also add
     corresponding Falsification Mechanisms for those claims before
     distribution.


Section 4 — Attribution and Negative-Result Citation

  a) You must give appropriate credit to the original authors, provide a link
     to this license, and indicate if changes were made. You may do so in any
     reasonable manner, but not in any way that suggests the licensor endorses
     You or Your use.

  b) If Your use of the Work produces negative, null, or inconclusive results
     that address a Covered Claim, You are requested (but not required) to
     report those results publicly. The licensor waives any right to suppress
     or contest the publication of such results.

  c) If Your Derivative Work removes or modifies a Covered Claim, You must
     document the original claim and the reason for its removal or modification
     in the FALSIFICATION.md file.


Section 5 — Anti-Suppression Clause

  a) No party may use patent rights, trade secret claims, non-disclosure
     agreements, or any other legal instrument to suppress the publication or
     distribution of:
     i.   Results that falsify or fail to confirm any Covered Claim.
     ii.  Source code or methods that implement Falsification Mechanisms.
     iii. Reproducible evidence contradicting the Work's predictions.

  b) If any provision of this Section is held unenforceable, the remaining
     provisions shall continue in full force and effect, and the parties shall
     negotiate in good faith to replace the unenforceable provision with a
     valid provision that most closely approximates the intent and economic
     effect of the unenforceable provision.


Section 6 — No Endorsement of Claims

  a) This license grants You permission to use and modify the Work. It does
     not constitute an endorsement of any Covered Claim by the licensor or any
     contributor.

  b) The Work may contain claims that are speculative, controversial, or
     contradicted by established science. You are encouraged — but not
     required — to accompany any distribution with an independent scientific
     assessment.

  c) Neither the licensor nor any contributor shall be held liable for damages
     arising from reliance on any Covered Claim. THE WORK IS PROVIDED "AS IS",
     WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT
     LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR
     PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT.


Section 7 — Copyleft

  a) Any Derivative Work that You distribute must be released under the Open
     Falsification License v1.0 or a later version approved by the licensor.

  b) You may not apply additional restrictions that violate the terms of this
     license, including but not limited to: restricting the right to publish
     negative results, requiring approval before publishing results, or
     conditioning access on agreement not to falsify Covered Claims.


Section 8 — Termination

  a) Your rights under this license terminate automatically if You fail to
     comply with any condition of Sections 3–7.

  b) Upon termination, You must cease all distribution of the Work and any
     Derivative Works. However, termination does not affect the rights of
     those who have received copies from You under this license, provided
     they remain in compliance.

  c) Rights may be reinstated if, within 60 days of termination, You cure
     all violations and notify the licensor in writing.


Section 9 — Versions

  The Free Software Foundation may publish revised versions of the Open
  Falsification License from time to time. Such new versions will be similar
  in spirit to the present version, but may differ in detail to address new
  problems or concerns.

  Each version is given a distinguishing version number. If the Work specifies
  that a certain numbered version of the OFL "or any later version" applies to
  it, You have the option of following the terms and conditions either of that
  numbered version or of any later version published by the licensor. If the
  Work does not specify a version number, You may choose any version ever
  published by the licensor.


Section 10 — Moral Statement

  Science advances through both confirmation and refutation. This license
  exists because the right to be wrong — and to prove others wrong — is the
  foundation of the scientific method. Any legal framework that protects claims
  from falsification is antithetical to science.

  By using this Work, You affirm that falsifiability is not a weakness but a
  strength, and that the most valuable result is not the one that confirms
  what we wish were true, but the one that reveals what actually is.


